# Monthly table maintenance review memo

Audit date 2026-09-01 was used for staleness, reindex validity, and change-control hold validity. Bloat ratios were computed as dead_pages / total_pages with round-half-up to 2 decimal places, and size_class was computed from total_pages only.

- T-82 is STALE_STATISTICS because computed large size from total_pages 1000 and dead_pages 80 gives ratio 0.08, which is within cap 0.10 tightened from 0.20, but stats are stale at 55 days since last analyzed; the legacy days_since_analyze field was ignored.
- T-13 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because autovacuum is disabled, with computed large size from total_pages 1000 and dead_pages 500 producing ratio 0.50 against cap 0.20.
- T-17 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because autovacuum is disabled, with computed large size from total_pages 1000 and dead_pages 400 producing ratio 0.40 against cap 0.20.
- T-72 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because manual vacuum overrides autovacuum even though autovacuum_enabled=True, with computed large size from total_pages 1000 and dead_pages 400 producing ratio 0.40 against cap 0.20.
- T-27 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because computed large size from total_pages 1000 and dead_pages 380 gives ratio 0.38, which exceeds the stale tightened cap 0.10 reduced from 0.20 after 46 stale stats days.
- T-04 is STALE_STATISTICS because computed large size from total_pages 1000 and dead_pages 100 gives ratio 0.10, which is within cap 0.10 tightened from 0.20, but stats are stale at 45 days sinc
